<title>RUSSIA: AGROKHLEB - Ukraine grain/sunseed output forecasts.</title>
<headline>AGROKHLEB - Ukraine grain/sunseed output forecasts.</headline>
<text>
<p>The following is a direct contribution from SovEcon Ltd, an independent research organisation specialising in agricultural production and trade in the former Soviet Union, in association with Ukragroconsult, a private Ukrainian agricultural consultancy based in Kiev.</p>
<p>UKRAINE: EARLY OUTLOOK FOR GRAIN AND SUNSEED OUTPUT IN 1997</p>
<p>MOSCOW, April 2 - SovEcon and Ukragroconsult's forecast for Ukraine's 1997 grain output is provisionally 34.0-34.5 million tonnes, including 1.5-1.8 million tonnes of minor cereals (beans, rice, millet, buckwheat).</p>
<p>Sunseed output is tentatively forecast in the range of 2.35-2.86 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Ukraine's spring grain plantings increased 23 percent on 1996, with maize (corn), oats and wheat seeing the biggest increases.</p>
<p>The increase reflects the growing responsiveness of producers to market signals and better adjustment of the sector to a new market environment.</p>
